{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates","id":818186,"title":"Can Freeholds be themed as anything but Feudal estates?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-27T21:16:54-08:00","id":818186,"title":"Can Freeholds be themed as anything but Feudal estates?","content":"ever used a Freehold that wasnt styled as a castle or country villa or some such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T00:24:00-08:00","id":818257,"title":"","content":"Looking at Freeholds and Hidden Glens, and Dreams and Nightmares, sure. Steampunk sprawl, early 19th century tavern, ornate garden, open glade in a residential building... freeholds aren't obliged to look like noble residences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:16:16-08:00","id":818370,"title":"","content":"Given the cause of the Resurgence, I think it would not be inappropriate for some Freeholds deeper in the Dreaming to be styled as 1960s zeerust space stations. Heck, you could have a &quot;Rocket Diner&quot; front in the mortal world that lets out onto a space scene in the Dreaming in the back. With TOS Star Trek command structure for the nobility running the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T19:40:55-08:00","id":819644,"title":"","content":"A character of mine once had a giant treehouse freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T20:14:15-08:00","id":819655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=818370#post818370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the cause of the Resurgence, I think it would not be inappropriate for some Freeholds deeper in the Dreaming to be styled as 1960s zeerust space stations. Heck, you could have a &quot;Rocket Diner&quot; front in the mortal world that lets out onto a space scene in the Dreaming in the back. With TOS Star Trek command structure for the nobility running the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Redcaps were enthusiastic about wearing red shirts until they realized that other kithain could miss them... and they'd still (chimerically) die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T10:21:11-07:00","id":997757,"title":"","content":"ohh was just curious? Ideas what a Childling can do with a Treehouse or playhouse freehold once hes outgrown it?<br /> <br /> Is gifting it to a new owner a good way to get boons, or thin k he could repurpose a freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:54:22-07:00","id":997896,"title":"","content":"Outgrowing a Freehold sounds like the most Banal thing ever.. I mean adult treehouses are a thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T19:22:36-07:00","id":998015,"title":"","content":"in &quot;the autumn people &quot; one of the banal Chimera is a Chimerical companion who was outgrown.<br /> <br /> Pg. 29 &quot;Celadyr&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T19:55:59-07:00","id":998581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=997896#post997896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outgrowing a Freehold sounds like the most Banal thing ever.. I mean adult treehouses are a thing</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible to become a person who is into something other than treehouses, though. Not exactly &quot;growing out&quot; of it, but over the course of life, people do change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:53:03-08:00","id":999960,"title":"","content":"Freeholds usually adjust themselves to their owners over time, so a tree house freehold might change to something the wilder would still enjoy. Our freehold is a Victorian-era bed and breakfast, dismantled and moved from Europe to America. It's also a combined dream / nightmare / twilight realm, depending on which &quot;reflection&quot; you end up in. It's a good idea to carry a mirror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T21:51:50-08:00","id":1000143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=997757#post997757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ohh was just curious? Ideas what a Childling can do with a Treehouse or playhouse freehold once hes outgrown it?<br /> <br /> Is gifting it to a new owner a good way to get boons, or thin k he could repurpose a freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either/or. I think it's more fitting to have the Freehold change with the controlling Changeling over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:03:36-08:00","id":1000339,"title":"","content":"I designed a Freehold once for a game that very consciously referenced a lot of Frank Lloyd Wright's architecture. Odd spatial relationships, use of natural surroundings, notes of retro-futurism, with a large indoor fire pit as the focal point to bring it back around to the idea of a medieval hall with a brazier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T23:57:05-08:00","id":1002141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates#post818186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ever used a Freehold that wasnt styled as a castle or country villa or some such?</div> </div> </div> </div> Why not a Theatre, a Circus, an Amusement Park,\u200b an Artist's Colony, an Ashram, a Commune, or a Spa? You need an organizing principle. Aristocracy was the old one. Feel free to experiment and watch the Sidhe murder you and ravage your dreamers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T22:37:40-08:00","id":1006004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1002141#post1002141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not a Theatre, a Circus, an Amusement Park,\u200b an Artist's Colony, an Ashram, a Commune, or a Spa? You need an organizing principle. Aristocracy was the old one. Feel free to experiment and watch the Sidhe murder you and ravage your dreamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Organizing Principle&quot;? Hmm . . . I think I'd describe it more as an &quot;inspirational work&quot;, dream, or work of art. Something that fires the imagination, and gets people thinking about the impossible. One strong enough to affect countless people. Graymere Glen, for example, feeds on every story/nightmare about a haunted &quot;evil&quot; lake in the woods, from <i>Beowulf</i> to <i>Friday the 13th</i>. While the Fool's Gambit (in Boston) draws from the American Revolution, the Sons of Liberty, and the Liberty Tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T13:23:26-08:00","id":1006833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1006004#post1006004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Organizing Principle&quot;? Hmm . . . I think I'd describe it more as an &quot;inspirational work&quot;, dream, or work of art. Something that fires the imagination, and gets people thinking about the impossible. One strong enough to affect countless people. Graymere Glen, for example, feeds on every story/nightmare about a haunted &quot;evil&quot; lake in the woods, from <i>Beowulf</i> to <i>Friday the 13th</i>. While the Fool's Gambit (in Boston) draws from the American Revolution, the Sons of Liberty, and the Liberty Tree.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Inspiration is the organizing principle. Circus, royal court, or doughnut shop, might be the form, horror movie, artwork, or childhood wonder, would be the principle. The form is the way you tell the story. \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T08:20:43-08:00","id":1031593,"title":"","content":"I realize this is something of an older post, but the short answer is yes. There are many different archetypes a freehold may be constructed around. The C20 core book touches on them briefly, and Book of Freeholds gets into the specific details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:31:49-08:00","id":1035382,"title":"","content":"One of the best choices might be a circus, there are a few still around, or a travelling performance troop. You'd need to make the Balefires (and you would need more than one) mobile. Travel would both give the Freehold political connections and adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T20:36:34-08:00","id":1035603,"title":"","content":"Old hotels, run down theaters (Neil Gaiman's The Last Temptation graphic novel springs to mind), former Prohibition speak-easies, forgotten underground subway stations from a hundred or more years ago, Roman era ruins, a used book store, an old boxing gym, an established neighborhood barbershop, all of them managed along the lines of what they are rather than on a sense of neo-feudalism. The Showman who runs the Theater of Forgotten Dreams may be the local Baron by title, but he still runs things like its a theater company.<br /> <br /> And the fun thing about old buildings and locations is that in the Dreaming they can regain their old glory and even exceed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:52:13-08:00","id":1035821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1035603#post1035603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Old hotels, run down theaters (Neil Gaiman's The Last Temptation graphic novel springs to mind), former Prohibition speak-easies, forgotten underground subway stations from a hundred or more years ago, Roman era ruins, a used book store, an old boxing gym, an established neighborhood barbershop, all of them managed along the lines of what they are rather than on a sense of neo-feudalism. The Showman who runs the Theater of Forgotten Dreams may be the local Baron by title, but he still runs things like its a theater company.<br /> <br /> And the fun thing about old buildings and locations is that in the Dreaming they can regain their old glory and even exceed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite true. A sense of style and a practical propose seem to make a strong combo. Reworked themes work too.<br /> <br /> Picture a once glorious old Hotel now shabby, but now it has a reputation for being haunted! The staff, many of them Changelings and relatives use mainly non-magical tricks and such to maintain the building's rep (with the rare bit of real Glamour thrown in to keep folks off balance). The glamour provided by thrill seekers keeps the place a strong freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:53:25-08:00","id":1036751,"title":"","content":"There is an Archetype of freehold that allows for multiple balefires, but they're pretty stationary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:34:31-08:00","id":1038613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1036751#post1036751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an Archetype of freehold that allows for multiple balefires, but they're pretty stationary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm certain Balefires could be carried in Circus Wagons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T20:46:02-07:00","id":1093088,"title":"","content":"I have a minor one that I used in when I had my group pass through my home town. Check out Valley of the Moon on the interwebs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T21:16:35-07:00","id":1093096,"title":"","content":"I don't think there actually are any more circuses in the United states. Ringling Brother's is on its farewell tour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T23:31:51-07:00","id":1093124,"title":"","content":"I thought most of the Freeholds mentioned in the books were things like Restaurants and bookshops? Say curious, what are the methods Changelings have for adding secret rooms that normally wouldn't fit into the physical space of a building?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T02:08:24-07:00","id":1093157,"title":"","content":"I've written scenarios for Spain and Chile. In Chile the european changelings have Freeholds of colonial style and baroque. The native changelings are influenced by the cultures mapuche, rapa nui and selknam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:28:53-07:00","id":1093208,"title":"","content":"This is a story seed that's been lurking on the back of my mind, but I think there's something to be said about how you could frame the feudalism of the fae as banal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:34:02-07:00","id":1093209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gl1tterboots</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1093208#post1093208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a story seed that's been lurking on the back of my mind, but I think there's something to be said about how you could frame the feudalism of the fae as banal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Maybe tie it in as that ruling structure right now came in with the Sundering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T07:06:53-07:00","id":1093224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1093209#post1093209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Maybe tie it in as that ruling structure right now came in with the Sundering.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With respect to how much of a miserable experience <i>actual</i> feudalism was, where the peasantry was stuck in a banal routine of drudgery with no opportunities or potential, I think it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T11:49:27-07:00","id":1093362,"title":"","content":"Oh goodness yes. In the game I run there are numerous freeholds around Malibu because, well, Malibu. One is a Spanish--style villa in Adamson House, but one is a little misfit cafe, one is a night club, there's a sort of faerie market, there's a series of strange underwater caverns beneath Malibu Pier for the Water Babies and their friends... freeholds come in all shapes and sizes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T22:58:01-07:00","id":1200720,"title":"","content":"Freehold in a game I'm running is really a coffee shop. But in the dreaming, it's a tavern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T15:18:08-07:00","id":1201017,"title":"","content":"A recent thread in the Wraith forum has me working on a Parisian Freehold, L'Maison d'Rue Morgue, made up of Poe enthusiasts with an interest in mystery and the macabre. Mostly members of House Eiluned, including Sidhe and Sluagh, as well as at least one Eshu, one Pooka and one Redcap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T15:27:20-07:00","id":1201018,"title":"","content":"A Primate Pookah. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T15:47:51-07:00","id":1201029,"title":"","content":"Heh. I'd considered a raven, but I'm also considering a Corax who lurks around from time to time as a potential crossover hook. Tentatively, she's a black cat who goes by the name of Cattarina Pluto (after Poe's cat of the same name and the title creature from &quot;The Black Cat&quot;).<br /> <br /> One of the Sidhe is of House Leanhaun, potentially named Annabel Lee.<br /> <br /> Added: The titular head of the Freehold is a Sidhe of House Eiluned, with the de facto leader being a Eiluned Sluagh Grump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 03-29-2018, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T22:59:58-07:00","id":1201151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1201029#post1201029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. I'd considered a raven, but I'm also considering a Corax who lurks around from time to time as a potential crossover hook. Tentatively, she's a black cat who goes by the name of Cattarina Pluto (after Poe's cat of the same name and the title creature from &quot;The Black Cat&quot;).<br /> <br /> One of the Sidhe is of House Leanhaun, potentially named Annabel Lee.<br /> <br /> Added: The titular head of the Freehold is a Sidhe of House Eiluned, with the de facto leader being a Eiluned Sluagh Grump.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The pooka has to be an Orangtan. I mean its that or become a librarian..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T18:52:00-07:00","id":1201501,"title":"","content":"The probably can.<br /> <br /> But consider the majority of Changelings who are in possession of one.<br /> <br /> Awful lot of Nobles, who don't approve of the modern world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:12:53-07:00","id":1203901,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve had an Unseelie Sidhe holding court from a freehold that was a modern Nightclub, located in the bustle of city central, with regular Satyr performers making sure that the cliantele there were less burdened by Banality. So that was kinda far from a feudal estate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:21:28-07:00","id":1204129,"title":"","content":"We have an abandoned speedway that is a Steampunk/Roman style roman Circus, they just finished the Ides of March Games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:52:33-07:00","id":1204202,"title":"","content":"Personally, after reading the crafting rules, I came to realise that everything in the dreaming that is not 'natural' has to be crafted by a Changeling. Which is why it mostly looks like mediaeval/renaissance construction techniques with the occasional bit of brickwork/steelwork in highly organised or populous areas.<br /> <br /> Changeling population is very very very low compared to human norms (maybe 1 in 10k at most by my estimate), even comparing the early middle ages to the modern age the human population is significantly less than 100 times more. This means almost everything needs to be made by hand for yourself, as it's quite difficult to find fae labourers for hire to build your manor house or work your mine or steelworks.<br /> <br /> There are no high tech modern labour saving devices - you can't drive a tractor into the dreaming and use it to farm chimerical potatoes, and there are no factories producing integrated circuits or electronics components. You don't have a petrol powered cement mixer or prefab wooden frames helping you build your house, you have to do every little bit by hand, including making the tools you need to harvest the materials in the first place.<br /> <br /> In short, for my stories, freeholds are 'feudal' styled because it's very difficult to build anything else, and I think that fits nicely with the Changeling themes. If the dreaming were totally malleable and you could make of it what you will then we'd just have another bland blend of anything goes that marks out mediocre fiction. I don't want Star Trek/Star Wars/Cyberpunk themed freeholds popping up and pissing about with the immersion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:38:49-07:00","id":1204734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1201501#post1201501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The probably can.<br /> <br /> But consider the majority of Changelings who are in possession of one.<br /> <br /> Awful lot of Nobles, who don't approve of the modern world.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Resurgence was fifty years ago. Very few nobles aren't part of the modern world. Sure there are fools that hunger for the 14th century. These are becoming fewer by attrition.<br /> <br /> Eventually the nobility's focus on aristocracy will engulf them in banality. Some will adapt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:47:33-07:00","id":1204740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1204734#post1204734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Resurgence was fifty years ago. Very few nobles aren't part of the modern world. Sure there are fools that hunger for the 14th century. These are becoming fewer by attrition.<br /> <br /> Eventually the nobility's focus on aristocracy will engulf them in banality. Some will adapt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No, they won't. Arcadian Nobles don't reincarnate (as far as we know), and when they made their grand return, the Freeholds defaulted back to them. The commoners tried to fight them back and ensure the continuation of a more modern society, but they lost. The Dreaming recognized and favored the aristocratic ideology of the Sidhe.<br /> <br /> It was only thanks to David giving them the privilege of holding titles that the Commoners were able to reclaim some of the territory the Sidhe forcefully took from them.<br /> <br /> And the deeper you go into the Dreaming, the more your Fae nature takes hold. C20 clearly points out that Nobles become increasingly less sympathetic towards Commoners as they progress through the Dreaming. By the time they get to the Deep Dreaming, they can barely tolerate being in the same room as each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-08-2018, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T20:07:13-07:00","id":1204774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1204734#post1204734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Resurgence was fifty years ago. Very few nobles aren't part of the modern world. Sure there are fools that hunger for the 14th century. These are becoming fewer by attrition.<br /> <br /> Eventually the nobility's focus on aristocracy will engulf them in banality. Some will adapt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The nonsidhe Kiths of Concordia were placing themselves into Feudal constructs at the time fo the Ressurgence so no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T20:34:27-07:00","id":1204777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1204774#post1204774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The nonsidhe Kiths of Concordia were placing themselves into Feudal constructs at the time fo the Ressurgence so no?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> More like they were forced into it. When the Sidhe showed back up, they told the commoners to hand everything over, and even though they refused, the Dreaming switched to their side anyways.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming prefers things to be run according to old ways. Which isn't surprising, as the new ways have only further encouraged Banality over the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T00:40:37-07:00","id":1204804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1204777#post1204777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> More like they were forced into it. When the Sidhe showed back up, they told the commoners to hand everything over, and even though they refused, the Dreaming switched to their side anyways.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming prefers things to be run according to old ways. Which isn't surprising, as the new ways have only further encouraged Banality over the centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, before the Sidhe showed up there were Pooka Dukes, Redcap kings, Troll barons etc. There still are but their percentage has greatly decreased. But before the Ressurgence there were a wide variety of various Kithain polities that rand the gamut of various real life structures.. much like the ACTUAL old days. Because before they left there wasn't this solid organized feudalistic only shit, there were complexties, voting monarchies, still active Republics and we had long since passed the time of Athens.<br /> <br /> The Ressurgence in Concordia imposed a unified false conceit on the continent. It also restored quite a variety of lost freeholds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:26:03-07:00","id":1205020,"title":"","content":"I have to confess, I have always found Changeling's vision of feudalism (at least that prior to War in Concordia) to be kind of dull when compared to the real life political shenanigans of places like the Holy Roman Empire, Plantagenet or Tudor England, or much of French history. <br /> <br /> As for non-feudal Freeholds, as Lian mentioned in another thread: Amusement Park!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T23:55:07-07:00","id":1205112,"title":"","content":"Back to the original topic:<br /> <br /> Currently we have a sidhe-free Freehold themed as a Nordesque longhouse situated in the Near-Dreaming representation of a city park's forested region, surrounded by ethernal spring.<br /> The Freehold is acessed by trods criss-crossing the park &amp; protected by several permanent enchantments.<br /> <br /> The Freehold is populated by multiple enchanted humans &amp; some Kithain &amp; Kinain, also with some Gallans. The ruling system is like the proto-democratic system of Iceland in the 1200s. The population are famed as sword for hire, mystics &amp; artisans (mainly weapon- and armorsmiths).<br /> The only other freehold nearby is an Unselee Nocker one, who produces mechanical contraptions. The relation is somewhat soiled but some trade-lines stand.<br /> <br /> The Freehold os sidhe-free because the ruler of the freehold (the go\u00f0i as we call it) is a Wolf-blooded relative of the Get of Fenris, who have free access to the longhouse... They stick to their bloodfeuds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T14:46:47-07:00","id":1205370,"title":"","content":"It has occurred to me that a small traditional urban barber shop, similar to the ones seen in Luke Cage, Coming to America or Barbershop, would make for an interesting commoner freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T14:58:49-07:00","id":1205376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1205020#post1205020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for non-feudal Freeholds, as Lian mentioned in another thread: Amusement Park!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, an amusment park COULD be a feudal freehold. You could get away with alot in the open that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:50:02-07:00","id":1205793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1205370#post1205370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has occurred to me that a small traditional urban barber shop, similar to the ones seen in Luke Cage, Coming to America or Barbershop, would make for an interesting commoner freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve used one as a Caern before so sure would be perfect!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:48:35-07:00","id":1206050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1205376#post1205376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, an amusment park COULD be a feudal freehold. You could get away with alot in the open that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this image in my head of a Princess Tea House full of assorted Sidhe, Pooka, Satyr and Boggin princesses. That and a &quot;Forgotten Futures&quot; pavilion full of Ethernaut Nockers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:54:12-07:00","id":1206054,"title":"","content":"Since Killerclown brought up private investigators in another thread, I think a detective agency (especially something along the lines of Bungo Stray Dogs or Blood Blockage Battlefront) would work pretty well as a commoner freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:54:30-07:00","id":1206055,"title":"","content":"Now that Book of Freeholds is out, the OP should have plenty of examples of freeholds that aren\u2019t feudal estates!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T18:36:23-07:00","id":1206218,"title":"","content":"Thanks to book of Freeholds we now have arena/Ludus where to become a Freeholder one must fight a dangerous Chimera on the sands!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T17:29:47-07:00","id":1206737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1206055#post1206055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that Book of Freeholds is out, the OP should have plenty of examples of freeholds that aren\u2019t feudal estates!</div> </div> </div> </div>Any examples you can share? (He said, making the most pathetic attempt at pleading puppy dog eyes ever seen by human kind.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T04:47:36-07:00","id":1206852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1206737#post1206737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any examples you can share? (He said, making the most pathetic attempt at pleading puppy dog eyes ever seen by human kind.)</div> </div> </div> </div>My favorite is Shamrocks Beer Cellar. I spent a lot of time role playing there back in the day and have so many fond memories of it. I was so happy to have a chance to revisit it.<br /> <br /> The American Indian Center really stretches the definition of freehold, but it shows off a sanctuary from Banality and how the Nunnehi can survive and even thrive in the face of overwhelming adversity.<br /> <br /> Underbridge and the Court of All Kings were a few old favorites to revisit.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m blanking on the name of these, but Steffie\u2019s example freehold she introduced in the opening fiction was an a joy to read. I also *love* the ranch that breeds flying alpacas!<br /> <br /> But yeah, the one in the book that I recall offhand as being anything like a traditional feudal estate is the Court of All Kings, and it\u2019s presented as incredibly dangerous ruins for an intrepid motley to rediscover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:35:59-07:00","id":1206917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1206852#post1206852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I\u2019m blanking on the name of these, but Steffie\u2019s example freehold she introduced in the opening fiction was an a joy to read. I also *love* the ranch that breeds flying alpacas!<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>. <br /> <br /> Cool, thanks \ud83d\ude42 (You know, there reallly should be a freehold farm somewhere breeding flying pigs purely to prove that all things are possible.) <br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not really all that in to most of the X20 material, but your description from here and the other thread makes me think that this is very much what I've long wished the original books on Freeholds, Haunts, Chantries, Caerns, and Havens had been like. Thanks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T14:39:21-07:00","id":1207017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1206852#post1206852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But yeah, the one in the book that I recall offhand as being anything like a traditional feudal estate is the Court of All Kings, and it\u2019s presented as incredibly dangerous ruins for an intrepid motley to rediscover.</div> </div> </div> </div>the Harajuku castle sounds pretty feudal... or at least one of the many &quot;I'm sure this is based on an anime trope..&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T15:16:45-07:00","id":1207031,"title":"","content":"Cool, I forgot one. There are probably others I forgot too. The book was written almost two years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:57:03-07:00","id":1208467,"title":"","content":"I think in terms of archetypical Freeholds for each Kith, Boggins would most certainly be the traditional tea house or some variation of it (bakery, bar that makes its own microbrews, etc.). I think there's actually one of such in San Fransisco (either the back of the 1st ed core book or Immortal Eyes: The Toybox).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T15:40:33-07:00","id":1208605,"title":"","content":"I liked the one that was a residential complex for just Kithain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T15:51:18-07:00","id":1208612,"title":"","content":"San Francisco was the original default city for Changeling. It\u2019s changed so much since \u201895 though. I wrote a small reference to the Toybox in Book of Freeholds, but I think it would be fun to have deep dive look at what those changes mean for the changelings in the city. It\u2019s too bad city books aren\u2019t really a thing anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T17:46:32-07:00","id":1208640,"title":"","content":"I think at one point there were plans for an Atlas of Concordia (back in the late 90s), but I never heard why it never came about. Such a thing would be kind of cool now, especially if it looked at a lot of the cities that'd already had books and so never would've had a Changeling sourcebook. Chicago, New York, LA, New Orleans, DC, Atlanta and Montreal. Plus places like Miami, Denver, Austin, Memphis, Toronto and others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T19:04:35-07:00","id":1208662,"title":"","content":"City books just don\u2019t sell well, and Changeling didn\u2019t sell as well as most of the other World of Darkness games back in the day. The combination of the two probably doomed that project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T19:49:58-07:00","id":1208679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1208662#post1208662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">City books just don\u2019t sell well, and Changeling didn\u2019t sell as well as most of the other World of Darkness games back in the day. The combination of the two probably doomed that project.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How well did Rage across the world sell? I'd love to see something like that and ti was fairly recent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T20:40:59-07:00","id":1208697,"title":"","content":"I know city books didn't sell well, but I was hoping that didn't mean Region Books didn't sell well. I would love an Atlas Concordia book! And have it kickstart a Global book series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T15:28:05-07:00","id":1209030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/818186-can-freeholds-be-themed-as-anything-but-feudal-estates?p=1208662#post1208662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">City books just don\u2019t sell well, and Changeling didn\u2019t sell as well as most of the other World of Darkness games back in the day. The combination of the two probably doomed that project.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what little I remember ever hearing about it was that it was, supposedly, going to be a chapter on each of the Kingdoms (Apples, Willows, Grass, etc.), what each of their Duchies were, some of the more important NPCs and plot hooks, and some other odds and ends, plus a look at the Parliament of Dreams. At least that's my decades old memories of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T15:50:49-07:00","id":1210174,"title":"","content":"I'm currently pondering the idea of a great mystic forge and armory in Pittsburgh (possibly Commoner independents, possibly not) that draws as much on the legend of Joe Magarac as it does on the likes of Weyland, Goibniu, Vulcan and such. Probably a population that is roughly 50% Nocker, 30% Troll and 20% Boggin. (The oldest Troll is probably missing an eye and is originally of Greek extraction.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, regarding theme parks, Seph Lawless's phono-book <b>Abandoned: Hauntingly Beautiful Deserted Theme Parks</b> is exactly as it describes itself, and strikingly symbolic of the bittersweet whimsey that Changeling can evoke at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 04-22-2018, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}